column5:
Chlorophyll a concentrations ranged from 0.3 to 45.1 µgl−1 with typical stages (Figure 2c). There were:
1. three years with peak concentrations (spring or late summer) around 20µgl−1 (1988–1990);
2. two years with maximal values for the study period, 45.1µgl−1 (in 1991) and 38. 5µgl−1 (1992, at the end of the summer season);
3. the last 4 years marked by a drastic decrease of pigment concentrations to an average of 5µgl−1, with spring peaks of under 10µgl−1.
